WEBVTT

1
00:00:01,401 --> 00:00:02,100
[The Breakfast Club
radio show plays]

2
00:00:02,102 --> 00:00:03,303
It's like that, Charlamagne.

3
00:00:04,171 --> 00:00:05,773
[laughing] You don't think it
kicks in immediately?

4
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:07,174
No, I don't think
it kicks in like that.

5
00:00:07,341 --> 00:00:08,408
The PEDs don't kick
in immediately?

6
00:00:08,576 --> 00:00:09,909
No, I don't think
it does like that.

7
00:00:09,911 --> 00:00:11,746
And I don't think
it guarantees that you'll hit
a home run.

8
00:00:11,913 --> 00:00:13,447
Charlamagne would do it
right before the game.

9
00:00:13,615 --> 00:00:14,849
-That's right.
-No.

10
00:00:15,015 --> 00:00:16,584
Now, uh, talk about
the rent in Brooklyn.

11
00:00:16,751 --> 00:00:18,586
Yes, so, the average rent
in Brooklyn now

12
00:00:18,753 --> 00:00:21,789
has soared up to $3,035.

13
00:00:21,956 --> 00:00:23,525
Is that crazy in Brooklyn?

14
00:00:23,691 --> 00:00:25,492
I don't know why anybody
would wanna live--

15
00:00:25,660 --> 00:00:26,761
In the best borough?
I don't know.

16
00:00:26,928 --> 00:00:27,896
For $3,000.

17
00:00:28,061 --> 00:00:29,263
That's $3,000 a month?

18
00:00:29,429 --> 00:00:30,665
-Yes!
-God...

19
00:00:30,832 --> 00:00:32,332
You don't even get grass
in Brooklyn.

20
00:00:32,499 --> 00:00:33,835
-Hell no.
-They do so have grass.

21
00:00:34,002 --> 00:00:35,200
You don't have no grass
in Brooklyn.

22
00:00:35,202 --> 00:00:36,971
You know what you can get
in Jersey for $3,000 a month?

23
00:00:37,137 --> 00:00:38,238
That's what I'm trying
to tell him.

24
00:00:38,405 --> 00:00:39,874
You know what you'd be getting
in North Carolina?

25
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,776
-Oh, Lord have mercy.
-Live like a king out there.

26
00:00:41,943 --> 00:00:43,511
We gon' buy
Fantasia's old house.

27
00:00:43,678 --> 00:00:44,779
[car engine revs]

28
00:00:44,946 --> 00:00:45,713
Wake up, man!

29
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:47,114
[cars honking]

30
00:00:47,281 --> 00:00:50,018
-[tires squealing]
-[crashing sound]

31
00:00:50,183 --> 00:00:51,249
[distant screaming]

32
00:00:51,251 --> 00:00:52,720
-[Man] Call an ambulance!
-[labored breathing]

33
00:00:52,887 --> 00:00:53,688
[Man] Sir, are you okay?

34
00:00:54,221 --> 00:00:55,623
[car engine revs]

35
00:00:55,790 --> 00:00:57,324
Hey. Hey, stop!

36
00:00:57,625 --> 00:00:59,092
Oh, my God!

37
00:00:59,794 --> 00:01:02,897
-[car engine revs]
-[tires squeal]

38
00:01:03,063 --> 00:01:04,732
[inaudible yelling]

39
00:01:09,269 --> 00:01:11,438
[record needle drops]

40
00:01:13,575 --> 00:01:18,211
♪ [Al Green's "Funny How Time
Slips Away" plays] ♪

41
00:01:23,017 --> 00:01:24,284
Oh, give me a hint.

42
00:01:24,451 --> 00:01:25,653
My favorite color.

43
00:01:25,820 --> 00:01:27,387
Favorite color's blue.

44
00:01:27,889 --> 00:01:29,222
-What?
-Blue...

45
00:01:29,924 --> 00:01:31,025
Blues singer?

46
00:01:31,191 --> 00:01:33,093
I can't believe you don't know
my favorite color.

47
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:35,362
-It's blue.
-No, it's green.

48
00:01:35,663 --> 00:01:37,065
Well, it used to be blue.

49
00:01:37,230 --> 00:01:39,067
No. Always green.

50
00:01:39,333 --> 00:01:40,868
Man, what a shame.

51
00:01:41,035 --> 00:01:42,637
Whatever. What's my
favorite color?

52
00:01:42,804 --> 00:01:43,838
-Purple.
-Ehh.

53
00:01:44,104 --> 00:01:45,573
-What?
-Lavender.

54
00:01:46,074 --> 00:01:47,240
Pshht. Same thing.

55
00:01:47,407 --> 00:01:48,943
Definitely not the same thing.

56
00:01:50,078 --> 00:01:51,779
[laughs]

57
00:01:51,946 --> 00:01:54,481
Oh, oh, oh! It's Al Green.

58
00:01:55,850 --> 00:01:56,718
Don't change the subject.

59
00:01:56,884 --> 00:01:57,952
You don't know
my favorite color.

60
00:01:58,118 --> 00:01:59,250
Well, you changed it first.

61
00:01:59,252 --> 00:02:00,855
You still haven't answered
my question about August.

62
00:02:01,421 --> 00:02:03,925
We gotta book a date soon
so we can get a deal.

63
00:02:04,525 --> 00:02:05,760
Yeah, August won't work.

64
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:07,160
Keith starts school.

65
00:02:07,327 --> 00:02:08,529
We gotta be there
to move him in.

66
00:02:08,696 --> 00:02:09,429
Mhm.

67
00:02:10,497 --> 00:02:12,399
-Mm-hmm.
-What?

68
00:02:13,034 --> 00:02:15,302
From foster care
to four year college.

69
00:02:15,937 --> 00:02:17,038
You did that.

70
00:02:18,472 --> 00:02:19,540
How's it feel?

71
00:02:21,876 --> 00:02:23,276
Can't wrap my head around it.

72
00:02:23,443 --> 00:02:24,444
Hmm.

73
00:02:24,712 --> 00:02:26,313
Gives me the chills
and makes me wanna cry

74
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:27,447
at the same time.

75
00:02:27,615 --> 00:02:28,482
Mm-hmm.

76
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:30,985
I just gotta make sure
he shows up.

77
00:02:31,786 --> 00:02:32,820
He'll show up.

78
00:02:33,253 --> 00:02:35,990
No, he's been through
too much not to show up.

79
00:02:36,557 --> 00:02:37,792
Yeah, I hope you're right.

80
00:02:39,527 --> 00:02:40,528
I am right.

81
00:02:41,629 --> 00:02:43,531
-Okay? Okay.
-Okay. Okay.

82
00:02:47,869 --> 00:02:48,903
Come on.

83
00:02:49,302 --> 00:02:50,337
Put the cake down.

84
00:02:50,505 --> 00:02:51,506
-What?
-Come here.

85
00:02:51,673 --> 00:02:52,874
-What you doing?
-Come here.

86
00:02:57,845 --> 00:02:58,880
[both] What?

87
00:02:59,047 --> 00:03:00,682
-Dance with me.
-Oh.

88
00:03:00,848 --> 00:03:01,816
Yeah.

89
00:03:01,983 --> 00:03:03,051
-Okay.
-Oh!

90
00:03:03,250 --> 00:03:04,852
Ooh, what was that?

91
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:10,190
You cannot dance like
that at our wedding.

92
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:13,861
Oh...

93
00:03:14,862 --> 00:03:18,198
Once your brother moves out,
we get our apartment back.

94
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,300
Mhm. True.

95
00:03:20,467 --> 00:03:22,269
-Our refrigerator.
-Mm-hmm.

96
00:03:22,503 --> 00:03:24,105
The bathroom.

97
00:03:25,472 --> 00:03:27,008
You get your car back.

98
00:03:27,508 --> 00:03:29,409
-Yes, I do.
-Mm-hmm.

99
00:03:35,717 --> 00:03:36,718
What?

100
00:03:38,418 --> 00:03:39,654
What if we moved?

101
00:03:39,821 --> 00:03:41,889
-Moved?
-It's so tight here.

102
00:03:42,355 --> 00:03:43,925
Well, baby, it is New York.

103
00:03:44,092 --> 00:03:45,159
Nobody has space.

104
00:03:45,358 --> 00:03:47,628
Nothing big is remotely
affordable anymore.

105
00:03:47,795 --> 00:03:49,329
Yeah, I can make
some more money.

106
00:03:50,198 --> 00:03:51,966
With Keith gone
and the market up.

107
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:54,035
My crew's hungry.
A few more projects...

108
00:03:54,202 --> 00:03:55,636
Baby, baby, baby.

109
00:03:56,037 --> 00:03:57,471
Listen to me.

110
00:03:58,005 --> 00:03:59,807
I don't care about more money.

111
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:02,342
Or the size of our apartment.

112
00:04:04,011 --> 00:04:05,213
I'm getting married.

113
00:04:06,581 --> 00:04:07,849
That's all I want.

114
00:04:08,983 --> 00:04:10,450
You and me.

115
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,689
I'm gonna build you
a house one day.

116
00:04:16,657 --> 00:04:17,792
You promise?

117
00:04:23,030 --> 00:04:24,297
From my own hands.

118
00:04:28,002 --> 00:04:29,871
You know how much
I love you, right?

119
00:04:33,174 --> 00:04:34,474
I really do.

120
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:41,381
♪ Shining so brightly ♪

121
00:04:43,818 --> 00:04:46,521
♪ It's me that's
missing your love ♪

122
00:04:49,824 --> 00:04:51,358
[banging on door]

123
00:04:53,828 --> 00:04:54,796
Who is that?

124
00:04:54,962 --> 00:04:57,430
[banging continues]

125
00:04:57,598 --> 00:04:58,633
What the...

126
00:04:58,933 --> 00:05:00,635
Who is knocking like that?

127
00:05:06,808 --> 00:05:08,109
[banging on door]

128
00:05:12,814 --> 00:05:13,881
[loud thud]

129
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:29,630
Keith? What happened?

130
00:05:29,964 --> 00:05:31,666
-[Keith sobbing]
-What happened?

131
00:05:32,432 --> 00:05:33,935
Bro. What happened?

132
00:05:34,802 --> 00:05:36,270
-I crashed.
-You crashed?

133
00:05:36,436 --> 00:05:37,638
You crashed in my car?

134
00:05:38,338 --> 00:05:40,107
Did somebody else get hurt?

135
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:41,776
They weren't moving.

136
00:05:41,943 --> 00:05:43,311
No! God.

137
00:05:43,476 --> 00:05:44,879
Keith, are they dead?

138
00:05:45,279 --> 00:05:46,379
They're dead.

139
00:05:46,547 --> 00:05:47,548
Shit!

140
00:05:47,715 --> 00:05:49,183
[distant police sirens]

141
00:05:53,988 --> 00:05:55,056
Keith, let me see.

142
00:05:55,223 --> 00:05:56,456
I can't let this happen.

143
00:05:57,357 --> 00:05:59,392
He'll be okay.
He'll be all right.

144
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:00,895
What are you doing?

145
00:06:01,062 --> 00:06:02,462
Why are you putting
on his shirt?

146
00:06:03,564 --> 00:06:05,132
-Chris. Stop it.
-Listen.

147
00:06:05,299 --> 00:06:06,300
-Stop it!
-Li-- no.

148
00:06:06,466 --> 00:06:07,768
He got a record, I don't.

149
00:06:07,935 --> 00:06:09,604
-Why are you putting it on?
-I can't let this happen.

150
00:06:09,770 --> 00:06:10,470
No!

151
00:06:10,638 --> 00:06:11,404
-Stop it.
Stop it.

152
00:06:11,572 --> 00:06:12,439
-Regardless he's going
to jail.

153
00:06:12,607 --> 00:06:14,208
He did it, Chris!
You didn't do it!

154
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:15,610
You don't know
what we've been through.

155
00:06:15,776 --> 00:06:16,544
What about me?

156
00:06:16,711 --> 00:06:17,979
You gotta trust me, baby.

157
00:06:18,145 --> 00:06:19,280
[sobbing] No, no.

158
00:06:19,446 --> 00:06:20,681
[police sirens]

159
00:06:21,115 --> 00:06:22,415
You can't do this.

160
00:06:29,857 --> 00:06:33,628
♪ [distorted "Funny How Time
Slips Away" plays] ♪

161
00:06:37,698 --> 00:06:40,134
♪ Shining so bright ♪

162
00:06:51,913 --> 00:06:54,382
[muffled yelling]

163
00:07:02,089 --> 00:07:03,524
[buzzer rings]

164
00:07:05,492 --> 00:07:06,459
Do you have a minute?

165
00:07:07,628 --> 00:07:09,030
[Woman] I need a big push,
Tara.

166
00:07:09,196 --> 00:07:10,131
[Tara screams]

167
00:07:10,298 --> 00:07:11,299
[Woman] Push!

168
00:07:11,464 --> 00:07:13,501
-[Tara screams]
-I can see it. Push, Tara.

169
00:07:13,768 --> 00:07:15,269
-That's it.
-[Tara groans]

170
00:07:15,435 --> 00:07:16,370
Push!

171
00:07:17,171 --> 00:07:18,873
That's it. That's it.

172
00:07:20,107 --> 00:07:22,810
[baby cries]

173
00:07:25,279 --> 00:07:27,815
[baby cries]

174
00:07:36,724 --> 00:07:39,093
Christopher Newborn,
the Queens, New York, man

175
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:41,629
convicted of felony
vehicular manslaughter

176
00:07:41,796 --> 00:07:44,999
after a hit and run in 2011,
is being released today

177
00:07:45,166 --> 00:07:48,169
after the Innocence Project
unearthed video evidence

178
00:07:48,336 --> 00:07:51,339
vindicating Newborn of
an additional murder charge

179
00:07:51,505 --> 00:07:54,041
stemming from a prison
fight in 2013.

180
00:07:54,275 --> 00:07:56,110
Records show Newborn
served nearly

181
00:07:56,277 --> 00:07:58,646
seven consecutive years
in isolation,

182
00:07:58,813 --> 00:08:01,382
placed there unjustly
by guards who framed him

183
00:08:01,549 --> 00:08:03,451
for the murder
of a fellow inmate.

184
00:08:03,617 --> 00:08:06,153
A murder committed
by those very guards.

185
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:07,855
Now, look, I wanna deal with

186
00:08:08,022 --> 00:08:09,623
the nightmare of him being

187
00:08:09,790 --> 00:08:11,258
thrown
into solitary confinement

188
00:08:11,425 --> 00:08:13,227
after getting framed
by these prison guards.

189
00:08:13,461 --> 00:08:14,929
Seven years in the hole.

190
00:08:15,096 --> 00:08:16,228
Seven.

191
00:08:16,230 --> 00:08:18,366
How does that impact
this brother's mental health?

192
00:08:18,532 --> 00:08:20,001
What does it mean
for his family?

193
00:08:20,167 --> 00:08:22,003
How can he get his life back?

194
00:08:22,203 --> 00:08:24,972
Newborn's case has not only
raised lawsuit flags,

195
00:08:25,139 --> 00:08:27,808
but has launched him into the
center of the ongoing debate

196
00:08:27,975 --> 00:08:30,378
over the inhumane
aspects of isolation

197
00:08:30,544 --> 00:08:32,046
within the prison system.

198
00:08:32,246 --> 00:08:34,915
[thunder rumbles]

199
00:08:35,449 --> 00:08:37,418
[rain patters]

200
00:09:02,576 --> 00:09:04,745
[thunder booms]

201
00:09:09,483 --> 00:09:10,818
[buzzer rings]

202
00:09:10,985 --> 00:09:12,920
[gated doors slide open]

203
00:09:14,822 --> 00:09:16,090
[reporter] Just over here.
One question!

204
00:09:16,257 --> 00:09:17,825
-Come on.
-[reporter] Chris, over here!

205
00:09:18,659 --> 00:09:20,694
[shouting overlaps]

206
00:09:21,262 --> 00:09:22,763
[reporter] Chris,
do you feel justice?

207
00:09:22,930 --> 00:09:25,599
Will there be a lawsuit
against the State of New York?

208
00:09:41,749 --> 00:09:44,685
[Tara laughs]

209
00:10:21,722 --> 00:10:23,023
Hey, Jake, get up here.

210
00:10:23,525 --> 00:10:24,526
Ready?

211
00:10:25,426 --> 00:10:26,528
Lean in, everyone.

212
00:10:26,694 --> 00:10:28,629
On one, two, three,
say cheese.

213
00:10:28,796 --> 00:10:29,697
[camera snaps]

214
00:10:30,264 --> 00:10:31,198
-Aww.
-[camera snaps]

215
00:10:35,736 --> 00:10:37,304
You swipe your finger.

216
00:10:40,107 --> 00:10:41,208
Like that.

217
00:10:44,546 --> 00:10:45,580
All right, buckle up, Jake.

218
00:10:46,981 --> 00:10:49,350
[car engine starts]

219
00:11:22,883 --> 00:11:25,786
[engine revs]

220
00:11:48,409 --> 00:11:49,611
[Chris] Still nothing.

221
00:11:49,777 --> 00:11:50,911
[Tara] He's been better.

222
00:11:51,845 --> 00:11:54,048
I mean, especially lately.
More responsive.

223
00:11:55,115 --> 00:11:57,686
They say he can come out
of it. That-that he...

224
00:11:58,319 --> 00:11:59,753
that he can talk.

225
00:12:00,522 --> 00:12:01,755
But...

226
00:12:02,756 --> 00:12:05,560
now the longer he doesn't,
the more chance he never will.

227
00:12:07,728 --> 00:12:09,330
What's that thing he squeezes?

228
00:12:09,763 --> 00:12:10,798
It's clay.

229
00:12:11,031 --> 00:12:12,900
It's part of clay art therapy.

230
00:12:13,067 --> 00:12:15,670
A doctor suggested it
a few years ago, and it stuck.

231
00:12:16,136 --> 00:12:17,639
And he just squeezes it?

232
00:12:17,805 --> 00:12:18,973
Sometimes, yeah.

233
00:12:19,139 --> 00:12:20,741
When he's coping
or calming down.

234
00:12:21,008 --> 00:12:22,644
He makes stuff too. See?

235
00:12:24,512 --> 00:12:26,013
My God. He did that?

236
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:27,114
Yeah.

237
00:12:27,281 --> 00:12:28,683
The way you're good at
building things,

238
00:12:28,849 --> 00:12:30,150
that's how he is with clay.

239
00:12:31,118 --> 00:12:32,286
Has it helped?

240
00:12:32,453 --> 00:12:34,255
With the, uh, the seizures?

241
00:12:34,421 --> 00:12:35,489
I think so.

242
00:12:36,423 --> 00:12:38,325
That and the-the medicine.

243
00:12:39,093 --> 00:12:40,995
No seizures so far this year.

244
00:12:48,836 --> 00:12:50,371
[voice on TV]
Come back here!

245
00:13:12,993 --> 00:13:14,862
You grew up on me.

246
00:13:17,331 --> 00:13:19,333
Last time I saw you,
you were--

247
00:13:22,737 --> 00:13:24,338
[Woody Woodpecker laughs on
TV]

248
00:13:25,939 --> 00:13:28,475
♪ [upbeat latin music plays] ♪

249
00:13:28,643 --> 00:13:31,912
[woman sings in Spanish]

250
00:13:36,083 --> 00:13:40,321
♪

251
00:13:42,791 --> 00:13:44,759
You used to love
to dance with me.

252
00:13:45,527 --> 00:13:47,227
You were never
very good, but...

253
00:13:47,861 --> 00:13:49,129
at least you tried.

254
00:13:50,164 --> 00:13:51,733
If I was bad back then...

255
00:13:52,801 --> 00:13:54,669
-Imagine now.
-I'm kidding.

256
00:13:56,870 --> 00:13:58,707
I love the way you move.

257
00:14:01,208 --> 00:14:02,510
I almost forgot.

258
00:14:08,082 --> 00:14:09,083
Open it.

259
00:14:12,787 --> 00:14:14,288
It's the first time
the three of us

260
00:14:14,455 --> 00:14:15,523
have been in
a picture together.

261
00:14:16,056 --> 00:14:17,491
Uh, Chris Newborn.

262
00:14:17,659 --> 00:14:19,026
So sorry to interrupt.

263
00:14:19,193 --> 00:14:20,194
Matt Walton.

264
00:14:20,762 --> 00:14:22,196
Look, I heard about
what happened to you,

265
00:14:22,363 --> 00:14:23,598
and I think it's just...

266
00:14:23,864 --> 00:14:25,999
awful, and I think the state
should be held accountable.

267
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:28,837
Now, my firm, Bregmen,
Foss and Associates,

268
00:14:29,002 --> 00:14:30,270
is both effective
and affordable--

269
00:14:30,437 --> 00:14:31,606
Not interested.

270
00:14:36,176 --> 00:14:37,244
Fair enough.

271
00:14:39,547 --> 00:14:40,715
Well, uh...

272
00:14:40,881 --> 00:14:42,751
I see you're enjoying dinner,
so I will just leave you

273
00:14:42,916 --> 00:14:44,218
my card, and if you do
change your mind--

274
00:14:44,385 --> 00:14:45,553
Not interested.

275
00:14:47,054 --> 00:14:47,955
Chris!

276
00:14:48,122 --> 00:14:49,423
We are not in danger, baby.

277
00:14:49,758 --> 00:14:52,192
Think about our family,
think about Jake.

278
00:14:55,764 --> 00:14:56,897
That's right.

279
00:14:57,832 --> 00:14:58,999
Now breathe, baby.

280
00:15:00,434 --> 00:15:01,669
Breathe.

281
00:15:13,347 --> 00:15:15,315
[lights buzz]

282
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:22,891
[doorbell buzzes]

283
00:15:29,329 --> 00:15:30,865
[man] You gonna let me in?
Or...

284
00:15:35,637 --> 00:15:37,104
Chris, what we doin'?

285
00:15:39,139 --> 00:15:40,374
I know you hear me.

286
00:15:49,016 --> 00:15:50,117
Welcome home.

287
00:16:04,097 --> 00:16:05,365
[Keith chuckles]

288
00:16:07,836 --> 00:16:09,169
My old digs.

289
00:16:11,606 --> 00:16:13,140
Memories in this place.

290
00:16:19,179 --> 00:16:20,414
How'd you know I got out?

291
00:16:20,582 --> 00:16:22,517
It's all they're
talking about on the news.

292
00:16:22,951 --> 00:16:24,953
Video of how they
framed you is everywhere.

293
00:16:26,119 --> 00:16:27,755
We always knew
you were innocent.

294
00:16:28,388 --> 00:16:29,591
Didn't make no sense.

295
00:16:30,625 --> 00:16:32,259
No one just snaps
and murders someone

296
00:16:32,426 --> 00:16:33,628
just before release.

297
00:16:34,696 --> 00:16:36,731
Saying you got a real
chance at a lawsuit.

298
00:16:37,599 --> 00:16:39,066
How it could be
in the millions.

299
00:16:40,602 --> 00:16:42,837
Saying how shocked they are
you survived the hole.

300
00:16:44,004 --> 00:16:45,372
I wasn't surprised though.

301
00:16:46,106 --> 00:16:47,140
Then again,

302
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:49,644
I know you.

303
00:16:52,112 --> 00:16:53,648
Nothing can break my big bro.

304
00:16:55,115 --> 00:16:56,083
Jake.

305
00:16:56,651 --> 00:16:58,252
Come say hi
to your uncle Keith.

306
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:01,723
How you doing, little man?

307
00:17:05,693 --> 00:17:07,762
Tara will be home
from work soon, so...

308
00:17:08,095 --> 00:17:10,097
And you don't want me around
when she gets here?

309
00:17:13,333 --> 00:17:15,068
I ain't ask you
to go away from me.

310
00:17:15,269 --> 00:17:17,070
-You didn't have to.
-Oh, right.

311
00:17:17,237 --> 00:17:18,238
'Cause that's what you do,
huh?

312
00:17:18,405 --> 00:17:20,307
-Keith.
-The heroic big bro.

313
00:17:20,474 --> 00:17:22,010
Flies in to save his
two-time loser brother.

314
00:17:22,175 --> 00:17:23,041
Can't do this right now.

315
00:17:23,043 --> 00:17:24,144
I guess I should be
saying thanks.

316
00:17:24,311 --> 00:17:25,279
Stop!

317
00:17:32,687 --> 00:17:34,288
Stop.

318
00:17:36,758 --> 00:17:38,593
Not exactly how
I thought this would go.

319
00:17:40,728 --> 00:17:42,162
I guess it is what it is.

320
00:17:46,233 --> 00:17:47,669
That's my cue, huh?

321
00:17:51,338 --> 00:17:52,540
All right, little man.

322
00:18:03,183 --> 00:18:04,318
[door closes]

323
00:18:10,525 --> 00:18:11,960
[Jake breathes heavily]

324
00:18:16,463 --> 00:18:17,464
[loud thud]

325
00:18:17,865 --> 00:18:19,199
Jake.

326
00:18:20,167 --> 00:18:21,569
-Hey, boys.
-Tara!

327
00:18:23,136 --> 00:18:24,672
T-Tara. I--

328
00:18:25,573 --> 00:18:27,609
Let's get you on your side.
All right.

329
00:18:27,775 --> 00:18:29,644
One, two, three.
All right, I got you.

330
00:18:29,978 --> 00:18:31,980
-Is he okay?
-He's all right.

331
00:18:34,448 --> 00:18:35,516
There you go.

332
00:18:36,050 --> 00:18:37,117
Look at me, baby.

333
00:18:37,919 --> 00:18:38,953
[Tara] Hey.

334
00:18:41,421 --> 00:18:42,690
Are you okay?

335
00:18:43,091 --> 00:18:44,191
[Tara] Just breathe.

336
00:18:45,258 --> 00:18:46,360
All right?

337
00:18:55,536 --> 00:18:56,738
How is he?

338
00:19:01,308 --> 00:19:02,409
He's fine.

339
00:19:04,311 --> 00:19:05,412
Just...

340
00:19:06,179 --> 00:19:07,749
mostly scared.

341
00:19:10,985 --> 00:19:12,486
I'm gonna ask you something.

342
00:19:14,187 --> 00:19:15,288
And...

343
00:19:17,491 --> 00:19:20,528
if you're not into it,
just say so.

344
00:19:21,562 --> 00:19:22,764
I'll be fine with it.

345
00:19:24,364 --> 00:19:25,967
How would you feel
about a trip?

346
00:19:30,303 --> 00:19:32,472
-A trip?
-Yeah. Like, uh...

347
00:19:33,975 --> 00:19:36,110
Like a break from the city.

348
00:19:36,276 --> 00:19:39,113
Someplace that has space
and fresh air.

349
00:19:39,346 --> 00:19:40,347
I--

350
00:19:40,848 --> 00:19:41,947
I don't feel comfortable,

351
00:19:41,949 --> 00:19:44,251
you paying for something
like that without my help.

352
00:19:45,485 --> 00:19:46,721
Ella's husband.

353
00:19:47,121 --> 00:19:48,623
He works real estate.

354
00:19:49,157 --> 00:19:52,259
The company he's with,
they own a resort up north.

355
00:19:54,128 --> 00:19:55,295
It's a quiet town.

356
00:19:55,763 --> 00:19:57,532
It's already closed
for renovations.

357
00:19:58,465 --> 00:20:00,702
She offered. Two weeks.

358
00:20:02,103 --> 00:20:03,671
There'll be no one
there but us.

359
00:20:05,506 --> 00:20:07,274
I think it could be
good for you.

360
00:20:09,110 --> 00:20:10,912
I think it could be
good for Jake.

361
00:20:14,381 --> 00:20:15,482
For us.

362
00:20:19,821 --> 00:20:20,922
A trip.

363
00:20:22,990 --> 00:20:24,058
A trip.

364
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:29,664
♪

365
00:21:23,217 --> 00:21:24,519
I'll assume you're Tara.

366
00:21:24,685 --> 00:21:26,053
-Tara. Yes.
-Tara.

367
00:21:26,220 --> 00:21:28,321
Ken Hershey.
Friends call me Hersh.

368
00:21:29,056 --> 00:21:30,057
Chris?

369
00:21:31,092 --> 00:21:32,527
You must be Big Jake.

370
00:21:32,994 --> 00:21:34,294
He's not much of a talker.

371
00:21:34,695 --> 00:21:36,931
You know that some of the best
men this country's ever known

372
00:21:37,098 --> 00:21:38,566
were men of very few words.

373
00:21:38,766 --> 00:21:40,300
Maybe while you're here,
you could be my extra

374
00:21:40,467 --> 00:21:41,869
set of eyes, sorta...

375
00:21:42,170 --> 00:21:44,705
like a junior
security officer.

376
00:21:44,872 --> 00:21:46,473
[Tara] Hmm. Oh...

377
00:21:46,641 --> 00:21:47,675
Take it.

378
00:21:50,711 --> 00:21:52,046
You got a special one there.

379
00:21:52,847 --> 00:21:54,682
You wanna have a look around?
Come on.

380
00:21:57,151 --> 00:22:00,788
We got two wings,
connected in the lobby here.

381
00:22:02,156 --> 00:22:05,226
The east wing is
the functional hotel
where you'll be.

382
00:22:05,793 --> 00:22:08,696
And, uh, west Wing, you can
see is down due to a reno.

383
00:22:08,863 --> 00:22:10,497
Nothing very exciting
to see there.

384
00:22:10,932 --> 00:22:12,233
Let's show you to your rooms.

385
00:22:13,968 --> 00:22:16,704
[ominous music plays]

386
00:22:22,310 --> 00:22:23,376
Oh.

387
00:22:24,444 --> 00:22:26,113
Oh, my God.

388
00:22:26,747 --> 00:22:28,082
It is gorgeous.

389
00:22:28,249 --> 00:22:30,051
[Hersh] Yeah. Imperial suite.

390
00:22:30,685 --> 00:22:32,286
I mean, uh, it's huge.

391
00:22:32,587 --> 00:22:33,386
Yeah.

392
00:22:33,754 --> 00:22:35,455
You mind if I steal Chris?

393
00:22:35,623 --> 00:22:36,858
Show him the rest
of the property.

394
00:22:37,058 --> 00:22:39,459
Uh, of course.
Yeah. I'll-I'll get, um...

395
00:22:39,627 --> 00:22:40,795
I'll get Jake settled in.

396
00:22:41,262 --> 00:22:42,597
I'll show you how
everything works.

397
00:22:43,197 --> 00:22:44,298
See you in a minute.

398
00:22:45,967 --> 00:22:48,135
Anything you can't handle
at all, just let me know.

399
00:22:48,302 --> 00:22:50,271
I'm just a mile south
down the main road.

400
00:22:52,173 --> 00:22:53,975
Being out of season,
not many people around.

401
00:22:54,208 --> 00:22:55,442
Wild animals?

402
00:22:55,676 --> 00:22:59,313
Oh, sure. We got raccoons,
and the odd wolf. Black bear.

403
00:23:00,181 --> 00:23:01,249
You probably won't see them.

404
00:23:01,414 --> 00:23:03,184
They mostly mind
their own business.

405
00:23:04,451 --> 00:23:06,020
So nothing too dangerous,
right?

406
00:23:06,754 --> 00:23:08,522
Nothing more dangerous
than you or me.

407
00:23:13,594 --> 00:23:15,796
[geese honking]

408
00:23:16,631 --> 00:23:18,366
[Chris] I guess you've been
wondering where I've been

409
00:23:18,532 --> 00:23:19,533
these past years.

410
00:23:21,335 --> 00:23:23,104
Why I wasn't here
with you and your mom.

411
00:23:28,910 --> 00:23:30,211
I made a decision.

412
00:23:32,613 --> 00:23:34,048
A decision I might've...

413
00:23:34,649 --> 00:23:37,351
considered differently had
I known you were on the way.

414
00:23:41,389 --> 00:23:42,590
I guess,

415
00:23:43,224 --> 00:23:44,992
I can't change the past,
but...

416
00:23:46,994 --> 00:23:50,463
What I can do is promise you
I will never leave you again.

417
00:23:52,199 --> 00:23:54,535
I will never let anything
happen to you.

418
00:23:56,604 --> 00:23:58,005
I love you, son.

419
00:24:00,241 --> 00:24:02,777
And your mother.
More than anything.

420
00:24:04,312 --> 00:24:06,914
And I'm gonna keep doing
the best I can to prove it.

421
00:24:17,992 --> 00:24:19,727
All right, uh...

422
00:24:22,196 --> 00:24:25,132
Let's get through this, uh,
once and if you don't like it,

423
00:24:25,299 --> 00:24:26,901
or if I'm no good at it,

424
00:24:27,168 --> 00:24:30,271
just pretend to fall asleep
or something. All right?

425
00:24:36,210 --> 00:24:38,813
Oh. You a comedian now.

426
00:24:56,931 --> 00:24:58,366
[Jake laughs]

427
00:25:22,890 --> 00:25:24,191
Do you like it here?

428
00:25:25,926 --> 00:25:26,927
Yeah.

429
00:25:27,828 --> 00:25:29,230
More than I thought I would.

430
00:25:31,032 --> 00:25:32,333
Yeah, me too.

431
00:25:34,402 --> 00:25:35,970
Reminds me

432
00:25:36,670 --> 00:25:39,508
that there's a whole world
outside of the city.

433
00:25:39,740 --> 00:25:41,275
Never thought I'd see the day
when the die-hard

434
00:25:41,442 --> 00:25:42,543
Queens native

435
00:25:42,710 --> 00:25:44,445
would entertain the idea
of leaving.

436
00:25:46,113 --> 00:25:48,849
All right, I'm always
gonna be from Queens, okay?

437
00:25:49,884 --> 00:25:50,918
-Okay?
-Okay.

438
00:25:51,085 --> 00:25:52,119
-Okay.
-Okay.

439
00:25:58,392 --> 00:26:01,262
Oh, my goodness, Jake,
this looks amazing.

440
00:26:01,530 --> 00:26:03,097
Did you do this
all by yourself?

441
00:26:48,577 --> 00:26:49,710
Look at you.

442
00:27:33,854 --> 00:27:35,189
What's wrong, baby?

443
00:27:36,023 --> 00:27:37,091
I don't know.

444
00:27:39,561 --> 00:27:40,562
Um...

445
00:27:41,829 --> 00:27:44,633
Oh... it's okay,
it's okay, it's okay.

446
00:27:44,798 --> 00:27:45,799
You're okay.

447
00:27:46,033 --> 00:27:47,501
It's okay. Okay?

448
00:27:47,668 --> 00:27:48,903
-Yeah.
-Look at me.

449
00:27:49,504 --> 00:27:51,438
-Yeah.
-You're with me, it's okay.

450
00:27:53,240 --> 00:27:54,308
Okay.

451
00:28:06,588 --> 00:28:07,656
Okay, baby.

452
00:28:08,322 --> 00:28:09,591
-Okay.
-I'm sorry.

453
00:28:09,757 --> 00:28:11,091
It's okay.
Don't be sorry.

454
00:28:11,325 --> 00:28:12,259
-I'm sorry.
-No.

455
00:28:12,426 --> 00:28:13,827
No, no, no, no,
don't be sorry.

456
00:28:13,994 --> 00:28:15,429
This is not your fault.

457
00:28:18,265 --> 00:28:19,333
We can...

458
00:28:21,536 --> 00:28:23,103
We can, we can wait.

459
00:28:24,071 --> 00:28:25,439
Until you're ready.

460
00:28:26,508 --> 00:28:28,742
It's just...
been a long time.

461
00:28:30,878 --> 00:28:31,979
I know.

462
00:28:41,455 --> 00:28:42,691
Have you, uh...

463
00:28:44,191 --> 00:28:46,293
thought-thought
at all about the...

464
00:28:47,728 --> 00:28:49,430
the lawsuit?

465
00:28:51,899 --> 00:28:54,636
-Lawsuit?
-Yeah, against, um, the state.

466
00:28:54,902 --> 00:28:56,303
The Bureau of Prisons.

467
00:28:57,338 --> 00:29:00,441
What-what they did
to you, baby,
what they did to you was,

468
00:29:00,609 --> 00:29:02,611
it's not right to our family.

469
00:29:02,776 --> 00:29:03,844
It is not right.

470
00:29:04,011 --> 00:29:05,246
Someone needs
to be held accountable.

471
00:29:05,412 --> 00:29:06,914
And if it's, if it's true,
what they're saying,

472
00:29:07,081 --> 00:29:08,749
that there could be
a settlement, that could--

473
00:29:09,584 --> 00:29:11,586
that could mean a new life.

474
00:29:13,053 --> 00:29:15,489
It could mean
more support for Jake.

475
00:29:16,257 --> 00:29:19,159
Give him the best chance
at the best treatment.

476
00:29:19,760 --> 00:29:20,861
Could--

477
00:29:21,596 --> 00:29:24,666
Could get us all
the help we need.

478
00:29:24,965 --> 00:29:26,735
I-I wouldn't, I wouldn't
know where to begin.

479
00:29:26,900 --> 00:29:28,536
Okay, baby, that's okay.

480
00:29:31,005 --> 00:29:32,507
I can do some research.

481
00:29:32,840 --> 00:29:35,710
You know, I could, I could
see what our options are.

482
00:29:41,915 --> 00:29:42,950
Okay.

483
00:29:44,485 --> 00:29:47,054
-Okay?
-Yeah. Okay.

484
00:29:49,557 --> 00:29:52,192
[muffled yelling]

485
00:29:56,163 --> 00:29:58,499
[lights buzz]

486
00:30:01,503 --> 00:30:02,570
Hello?

487
00:30:40,474 --> 00:30:43,043
[breathing heavily]

488
00:31:34,962 --> 00:31:36,698
[car horn honks]

489
00:32:03,725 --> 00:32:06,795
-[Tara laughs]
-[indistinct conversation]

490
00:32:06,960 --> 00:32:08,095
-[Tara laughs]
-[Hersh] Yeah.

491
00:32:08,262 --> 00:32:08,996
[both] Hey.

492
00:32:09,764 --> 00:32:10,732
Hey.

493
00:32:11,265 --> 00:32:12,433
Yeah, I brought you
some goodies.

494
00:32:12,600 --> 00:32:13,668
Some veggies from the garden.

495
00:32:13,835 --> 00:32:14,769
Where's Jake?

496
00:32:15,770 --> 00:32:17,104
Uh, inside.

497
00:32:19,574 --> 00:32:21,408
You, uh, settling in okay?

498
00:32:21,975 --> 00:32:23,477
Yeah. Just fine.

499
00:32:24,378 --> 00:32:26,648
Well, you chose a beautiful
day for a jog.

500
00:32:30,050 --> 00:32:31,753
All right, I'm gonna head out.

501
00:32:31,920 --> 00:32:34,021
Finish binge-watching Ozark.

502
00:32:34,955 --> 00:32:35,989
If you need me, I'm just--

503
00:32:36,156 --> 00:32:38,058
A mile south on the main road.
Yeah, we know.

504
00:32:38,392 --> 00:32:39,894
All right.

505
00:32:42,362 --> 00:32:44,331
-[Tara] Thanks.
-You bet.

506
00:32:46,801 --> 00:32:48,703
[truck engine starts]

507
00:32:49,571 --> 00:32:51,539
[truck pulls away]

508
00:32:55,142 --> 00:32:56,310
That was rude.

509
00:32:58,111 --> 00:32:59,647
There's something about him.

510
00:32:59,948 --> 00:33:01,148
I don't know.

511
00:33:03,417 --> 00:33:04,985
Let me know when
he comes around, okay?

512
00:33:06,053 --> 00:33:07,589
Yeah. Okay.

513
00:33:11,024 --> 00:33:13,795
[muffled yelling]

514
00:34:20,127 --> 00:34:22,797
I got a letter from your mom
when you turned five.

515
00:34:24,398 --> 00:34:26,466
They'd been blocking
my mail for years.

516
00:34:27,802 --> 00:34:29,136
But this one got through.

517
00:34:30,638 --> 00:34:32,472
She said you still
hadn't spoke yet.

518
00:34:33,575 --> 00:34:35,175
And I knew that was on me.

519
00:34:36,711 --> 00:34:38,478
The world being what it is,

520
00:34:39,881 --> 00:34:41,583
if I had just
been there for you,

521
00:34:42,684 --> 00:34:45,152
maybe things would've
been different.

522
00:34:48,823 --> 00:34:51,158
You're my mission.
You know that?

523
00:34:52,594 --> 00:34:54,929
From now on, we face
the world together, aight?

524
00:35:00,001 --> 00:35:01,636
Did you just give me
a direct answer?

525
00:35:27,929 --> 00:35:31,733
Two years in, days from
release, you intervene
as guards

526
00:35:31,899 --> 00:35:33,901
beat a man to death.

527
00:35:34,669 --> 00:35:37,939
This is video that has been
widely circulated

528
00:35:38,106 --> 00:35:40,108
which proves you acted
in self-defense.

529
00:35:41,976 --> 00:35:43,811
If those men didn't
frame you, Chris,

530
00:35:43,978 --> 00:35:46,114
you would've been headed home
to be with your family.

531
00:35:46,279 --> 00:35:48,049
Instead, you get
a life sentence.

532
00:35:48,482 --> 00:35:50,084
Worse, to hide their crimes,

533
00:35:50,250 --> 00:35:52,887
they bury you in solitary
confinement to be forgotten.

534
00:35:53,888 --> 00:35:56,024
No visitation, no programs.

535
00:35:56,189 --> 00:35:58,392
Seven years of hell.

536
00:35:59,661 --> 00:36:00,962
Those are the details.

537
00:36:01,129 --> 00:36:04,231
Details that will give
the court just a small idea

538
00:36:04,632 --> 00:36:06,466
of the tragedy
that you've endured.

539
00:36:19,814 --> 00:36:21,181
[buzzer rings]

540
00:36:21,348 --> 00:36:22,684
[steel doors slide open]

541
00:36:23,216 --> 00:36:25,520
[men yelling]

542
00:36:26,654 --> 00:36:28,756
I'm ready to kill
somebody today!

543
00:36:28,923 --> 00:36:30,124
You think you can touch me?

544
00:36:30,290 --> 00:36:32,960
Come get me!
You cannot come in here!

545
00:36:33,127 --> 00:36:34,294
Come get me! Come!

546
00:37:05,560 --> 00:37:08,428
[stapler gun clacks]

547
00:37:10,230 --> 00:37:12,734
[saw buzzes]

548
00:37:18,039 --> 00:37:20,775
[sander grinding]

549
00:37:39,761 --> 00:37:42,329
[vehicle approaches]

550
00:37:46,701 --> 00:37:48,903
[vehicle door opens and
closes]

551
00:37:49,504 --> 00:37:51,205
[vehicle drives off]

552
00:37:59,247 --> 00:38:00,915
What the hell
are you doing here?

553
00:38:02,382 --> 00:38:03,584
Great to see you, too.

554
00:38:03,751 --> 00:38:04,685
Who brought you here?

555
00:38:05,086 --> 00:38:06,453
You need to call him back.

556
00:38:09,724 --> 00:38:11,526
What is this, déjà vu?

557
00:38:14,695 --> 00:38:15,797
Of course you're high.

558
00:38:16,697 --> 00:38:18,132
Come on, get inside.

559
00:38:23,470 --> 00:38:24,839
-[loud thud]
-[gasps]

560
00:38:37,185 --> 00:38:38,286
No suite?

561
00:38:39,921 --> 00:38:41,454
Whoever brought you here,
you need to call him

562
00:38:41,622 --> 00:38:42,757
to come get you.

563
00:38:44,859 --> 00:38:46,694
You at all curious
how this happened?

564
00:38:47,061 --> 00:38:48,963
Something to do with
the needle marks on your arm?

565
00:38:50,665 --> 00:38:52,099
Someone came looking for you.

566
00:38:53,466 --> 00:38:54,635
Day after I saw you.

567
00:38:55,203 --> 00:38:57,205
-Looking for me?
-Two guys.

568
00:38:58,072 --> 00:38:59,507
They knew I was your brother.

569
00:38:59,674 --> 00:39:01,576
Looked like they could've
been law enforcement.

570
00:39:01,976 --> 00:39:03,544
Asked questions about you.

571
00:39:04,212 --> 00:39:05,213
Me.

572
00:39:05,813 --> 00:39:07,447
-Our family.
-What'd you tell 'em?

573
00:39:12,553 --> 00:39:14,454
It would've been worse,
but I ran.

574
00:39:19,694 --> 00:39:20,828
How'd you know I was here?

575
00:39:20,995 --> 00:39:22,897
Tara told the neighbor
across the hall.

576
00:39:23,664 --> 00:39:25,132
In case of emergency.

577
00:39:26,901 --> 00:39:28,002
These guys...

578
00:39:28,536 --> 00:39:30,338
I think they had something
to do with your case.

579
00:39:38,478 --> 00:39:39,513
Hey, son.

580
00:39:40,715 --> 00:39:42,382
What you doing here,
you can't sleep?

581
00:39:46,187 --> 00:39:48,656
Uncle Keith may stay here
for a few days.

582
00:39:48,956 --> 00:39:50,791
Uh... he's sick,

583
00:39:51,125 --> 00:39:52,894
and we're gonna
look after him, aight?

584
00:39:53,628 --> 00:39:54,996
What up, nephew?

585
00:39:56,597 --> 00:39:58,465
Probably best we don't tell
your mom about this.

586
00:39:58,633 --> 00:40:00,635
I got a feeling he's not
the snitching type.

587
00:40:00,801 --> 00:40:02,904
She might not think he's
the best influence on you.

588
00:40:06,406 --> 00:40:07,675
Come on, let's head back.

589
00:40:10,378 --> 00:40:11,379
Chris.

590
00:40:13,214 --> 00:40:14,548
No matter what happens,

591
00:40:15,683 --> 00:40:17,051
just keep Jake safe.

592
00:40:18,586 --> 00:40:19,620
Safe from who?

593
00:40:21,322 --> 00:40:22,390
Everyone.

594
00:40:25,693 --> 00:40:28,095
Your Uncle Keith,
he was the type of kid

595
00:40:28,262 --> 00:40:30,364
that after he watched
a superhero movie,

596
00:40:30,598 --> 00:40:32,533
he became that character.

597
00:40:32,700 --> 00:40:34,135
Superpowers and all.

598
00:40:35,169 --> 00:40:38,506
This one time,
he's like... six.

599
00:40:38,773 --> 00:40:41,208
We're home alone
watching Spider-Man.

600
00:40:41,642 --> 00:40:43,644
And within five minutes,
he's climbing the walls.

601
00:40:43,811 --> 00:40:46,414
So, I'm thinking...
he's occupied.

602
00:40:46,881 --> 00:40:48,316
So, I started doing
my homework.

603
00:40:48,481 --> 00:40:49,550
Little did I know,

604
00:40:49,717 --> 00:40:52,219
that this genius has
unplugged the cable cord,

605
00:40:52,386 --> 00:40:54,355
and tied it to this huge
"if you touch it,

606
00:40:54,522 --> 00:40:56,023
we will kill you"
china cabinet.

607
00:40:56,190 --> 00:40:57,658
Nuh-uh. [laughs]

608
00:40:58,092 --> 00:40:59,794
So, I'm studying or whatever,

609
00:40:59,961 --> 00:41:02,196
and I hear what sounds like
a truck crashing

610
00:41:02,363 --> 00:41:03,463
in the front room.

611
00:41:03,798 --> 00:41:06,400
So, I run in there,
and here's Keith.

612
00:41:06,901 --> 00:41:08,569
Spider-Man underwear on,

613
00:41:08,869 --> 00:41:11,172
stocking over his head,
standing over this

614
00:41:11,339 --> 00:41:14,408
collapsed china cabinet
and broken glass everywhere.

615
00:41:14,575 --> 00:41:15,776
Oh, no.

616
00:41:16,010 --> 00:41:16,811
-It gets worse.
-Nuh-uh.

617
00:41:16,978 --> 00:41:17,745
It gets worse.

618
00:41:17,912 --> 00:41:19,347
At exactly that moment,

619
00:41:19,914 --> 00:41:22,316
our foster parents' car
pulls up in the driveway.

620
00:41:22,482 --> 00:41:23,818
Oh, God.
What did you do?

621
00:41:24,185 --> 00:41:25,853
Would any sensible
11 year old would do.

622
00:41:26,020 --> 00:41:27,254
I knocked some pictures
off the wall,

623
00:41:27,421 --> 00:41:28,556
told 'em it was
an earthquake.

624
00:41:28,723 --> 00:41:29,857
[laughs] In Brooklyn.

625
00:41:30,024 --> 00:41:31,158
Made sense in my head.

626
00:41:32,827 --> 00:41:34,028
But, yeah.

627
00:41:34,494 --> 00:41:36,764
We didn't last much longer
with that family.

628
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:40,668
[phone buzzes and pings]

629
00:41:46,874 --> 00:41:47,742
You good?

630
00:41:48,209 --> 00:41:49,343
Yeah. [laughs]

631
00:41:50,311 --> 00:41:51,812
I'm gonna use the ladies room.

632
00:41:53,147 --> 00:41:55,082
Don't get any ideas
from your father.

633
00:41:55,583 --> 00:41:56,951
[Tara chuckles]

634
00:41:58,052 --> 00:41:59,553
[door bell rings]

635
00:42:30,551 --> 00:42:32,053
Hey, Jake. Come on.

636
00:42:39,860 --> 00:42:40,928
Hey!

637
00:42:44,865 --> 00:42:46,367
[ticking sound]

638
00:42:47,001 --> 00:42:48,469
[muted dialogue]

639
00:42:49,437 --> 00:42:52,106
[men yelling]

640
00:42:59,380 --> 00:43:01,282
[yelling intensifies]

641
00:43:22,837 --> 00:43:24,238
[police radio chatter]

642
00:43:50,397 --> 00:43:51,832
I got a call.

643
00:43:53,400 --> 00:43:54,502
From Ella.

644
00:43:56,871 --> 00:43:58,205
She needed to talk.

645
00:43:58,873 --> 00:44:00,575
I shouldn't have left you,
I just--

646
00:44:01,842 --> 00:44:02,943
I'm sorry.

647
00:44:04,945 --> 00:44:06,013
Hersh.

648
00:44:07,281 --> 00:44:08,682
How'd he know we were here?

649
00:44:09,850 --> 00:44:10,851
I called him.

650
00:44:12,587 --> 00:44:13,555
You have his number?

651
00:44:14,155 --> 00:44:16,090
He gave it to us both, Cris.

652
00:44:18,325 --> 00:44:20,094
They would've arrested you.
I--

653
00:44:21,028 --> 00:44:23,697
I figured he could help.

654
00:45:01,902 --> 00:45:03,204
Change of clothes.

655
00:45:15,916 --> 00:45:17,718
What you mean by
what you said last night?

656
00:45:19,588 --> 00:45:21,188
About keeping Jake safe?

657
00:45:24,526 --> 00:45:26,327
The guys who came
looking for you.

658
00:45:29,930 --> 00:45:31,432
They asked about you.

659
00:45:33,934 --> 00:45:34,935
And Jake.

660
00:45:39,574 --> 00:45:41,208
But they never asked
where you were.

661
00:45:46,380 --> 00:45:48,282
They just told me
to stay away from you.

662
00:45:52,186 --> 00:45:53,887
That they wanted you
to be alone.

663
00:45:56,957 --> 00:45:58,092
Isolated.

664
00:46:00,361 --> 00:46:01,996
Vulnerable.

665
00:46:04,465 --> 00:46:06,433
That's why I knew
I had to come find you.

666
00:46:10,804 --> 00:46:12,773
So whatever they were
coming at you with,

667
00:46:14,074 --> 00:46:15,677
you wouldn't have to
face 'em alone.

668
00:46:24,552 --> 00:46:26,320
I had a dream I OD'd.

669
00:46:29,591 --> 00:46:31,225
I'm tired of this ride, bro.

670
00:46:35,597 --> 00:46:36,830
I'm ready to get off.

671
00:47:17,404 --> 00:47:18,439
Hey.

672
00:47:19,473 --> 00:47:20,474
Hey.

673
00:47:20,709 --> 00:47:22,276
-Mmm.
-Where are you?

674
00:47:36,323 --> 00:47:37,458
What did I do?

675
00:47:48,035 --> 00:47:50,772
I feel, I feel so alone here.

676
00:47:54,408 --> 00:47:57,978
Let the two of us on,
on two separate trips.

677
00:48:00,447 --> 00:48:02,249
I know. Hey, I know, I know.

678
00:48:03,417 --> 00:48:04,652
I know there's
a lot that you're

679
00:48:04,819 --> 00:48:05,986
still trying to figure out.

680
00:48:06,153 --> 00:48:07,988
And I don't wanna
get in the way of that.

681
00:48:09,824 --> 00:48:11,091
What do you want?

682
00:48:15,630 --> 00:48:16,798
Your love.

683
00:48:19,032 --> 00:48:20,033
That's all.

684
00:48:23,137 --> 00:48:24,506
Do you love me still?

685
00:48:27,742 --> 00:48:28,743
Yeah.

686
00:48:29,878 --> 00:48:30,978
I love you.

687
00:48:40,020 --> 00:48:41,088
Yeah, okay.

688
00:48:44,091 --> 00:48:45,092
Okay.

689
00:48:46,861 --> 00:48:47,896
Okay.

690
00:49:03,944 --> 00:49:05,847
[crickets chirping]

691
00:49:06,714 --> 00:49:08,750
[seagull caws]

692
00:49:37,846 --> 00:49:39,213
[buzzer rings]

693
00:49:39,379 --> 00:49:40,582
[muffled announcement]

694
00:50:03,972 --> 00:50:05,507
If you've seen it
in your mind,

695
00:50:05,974 --> 00:50:08,141
you can create it
and you can get there

696
00:50:09,711 --> 00:50:11,245
from right here.

697
00:50:13,715 --> 00:50:15,115
Protect your mind, son.

698
00:50:15,950 --> 00:50:17,284
It's your greatest asset.

699
00:50:18,887 --> 00:50:20,053
Hey.

700
00:50:21,823 --> 00:50:24,926
You don't let nobody walk
through it with dirty feet.

701
00:50:25,960 --> 00:50:27,027
You hear me?

702
00:50:28,395 --> 00:50:31,265
Protect your mind.

703
00:50:35,302 --> 00:50:36,938
-[gunshot]
-[bullet whizzes by]

704
00:51:01,796 --> 00:51:02,830
We're here.

705
00:51:03,865 --> 00:51:04,899
Stay close.

706
00:51:46,373 --> 00:51:48,241
Your life just got spared,
sir.

707
00:51:54,616 --> 00:51:56,416
Man, I don't know how
it works in the city, but...

708
00:51:56,584 --> 00:51:57,719
trespassing around here

709
00:51:57,885 --> 00:51:59,554
usually ends with
a pine box and nails.

710
00:51:59,721 --> 00:52:01,089
We got shot at today.

711
00:52:03,190 --> 00:52:05,026
You get shot at
in these woods here?

712
00:52:05,560 --> 00:52:06,561
Yeah.

713
00:52:07,829 --> 00:52:09,664
-In these woods?
-In these woods.

714
00:52:09,831 --> 00:52:11,331
This afternoon.

715
00:52:13,233 --> 00:52:14,736
Well, that's odd,
Chris, 'cause...

716
00:52:15,168 --> 00:52:16,638
not many people
around here.

717
00:52:18,673 --> 00:52:20,340
Nobody hunts
around here but me.

718
00:52:21,943 --> 00:52:23,210
And were you hunting?

719
00:52:24,846 --> 00:52:25,980
This afternoon?

720
00:52:32,452 --> 00:52:33,588
Come on, Jake.

721
00:52:37,257 --> 00:52:39,226
I'm not sure how it
works in the country,

722
00:52:39,894 --> 00:52:41,095
but in the city,

723
00:52:41,629 --> 00:52:43,564
when someone shoots at you,
you don't wait for it

724
00:52:43,731 --> 00:52:44,832
to happen again.

725
00:52:50,705 --> 00:52:51,739
Hey.

726
00:52:54,174 --> 00:52:55,576
You be careful out there.

727
00:53:04,317 --> 00:53:05,419
You too.

728
00:53:40,988 --> 00:53:42,123
Can I help you?

729
00:53:43,191 --> 00:53:44,959
Yeah, yeah. Uh...

730
00:53:45,425 --> 00:53:46,561
my son here.

731
00:53:47,494 --> 00:53:48,696
His first season.

732
00:53:49,197 --> 00:53:50,531
Uh, looking for a rifle.

733
00:53:51,165 --> 00:53:52,567
Summer hunting or fall?

734
00:53:53,000 --> 00:53:54,001
What's-what's the difference?

735
00:53:54,168 --> 00:53:55,536
Oh, just the game. Uh...

736
00:53:56,170 --> 00:53:57,171
maybe the caliber.

737
00:53:57,370 --> 00:54:00,174
We got red squirrels,
sparrows, starlings,

738
00:54:00,340 --> 00:54:02,476
rock pigeons,
monk parakeets.

739
00:54:02,643 --> 00:54:04,679
Of course, come fall,
you got everything else.

740
00:54:04,879 --> 00:54:06,781
We're going to be hunting
bigger game, so, uh...

741
00:54:07,247 --> 00:54:08,348
I'd say fall.

742
00:54:08,950 --> 00:54:10,218
Deer or bear?

743
00:54:10,551 --> 00:54:12,820
Yeah. Uh... deer.

744
00:54:12,987 --> 00:54:14,589
Okay, well,
then you're probably looking

745
00:54:14,756 --> 00:54:16,456
for a mid-size caliber.

746
00:54:18,926 --> 00:54:22,063
That is a, uh, Browning
A-Bolt, extended barrel.

747
00:54:23,164 --> 00:54:24,899
You can hit a buck
a hundred yards away.

748
00:54:25,066 --> 00:54:26,033
Barely no slope.

749
00:54:27,135 --> 00:54:28,169
Yeah, I'll take it.

750
00:54:29,537 --> 00:54:31,371
Uh... good deal.

751
00:54:32,039 --> 00:54:35,375
Uh, I'm gonna need to see
some ID and a game license.

752
00:54:39,580 --> 00:54:40,782
Oh...

753
00:54:42,517 --> 00:54:44,819
You didn't grab Daddy's wallet
off the counter, did you?

754
00:54:46,521 --> 00:54:47,522
Oh, man.

755
00:54:47,755 --> 00:54:48,856
Um.

756
00:54:49,389 --> 00:54:50,457
You know what?

757
00:54:50,792 --> 00:54:52,226
My wife's card.

758
00:54:52,693 --> 00:54:54,595
I used it to grab some
groceries this morning.

759
00:54:54,762 --> 00:54:56,363
Maybe I could use this
for now?

760
00:54:56,531 --> 00:54:59,133
Bring back my paperwork
in the next day or so?

761
00:55:02,236 --> 00:55:03,638
You don't have no ID.

762
00:55:04,471 --> 00:55:06,507
You don't have a game license
or a money card

763
00:55:06,674 --> 00:55:08,042
with your name on it.

764
00:55:08,943 --> 00:55:11,378
And you want me to let you
walk outta here with a rifle?

765
00:55:35,303 --> 00:55:36,704
Let's get you in the car.

766
00:55:53,020 --> 00:55:54,288
If they're here,

767
00:55:54,789 --> 00:55:56,557
that mean we all
in danger, right?

768
00:55:58,559 --> 00:56:00,161
Maybe we tell Tara I'm here.

769
00:56:01,629 --> 00:56:02,997
Pissed as she might be,

770
00:56:03,396 --> 00:56:05,132
at least I'll be on
that side with you.

771
00:56:08,135 --> 00:56:09,337
I'm not scared.

772
00:56:09,937 --> 00:56:11,438
I'm just saying.

773
00:56:12,773 --> 00:56:14,275
Or maybe we call the cops.

774
00:56:15,309 --> 00:56:16,409
Cops?

775
00:56:17,044 --> 00:56:18,112
[scoffs]

776
00:56:18,279 --> 00:56:19,881
Don't think Hersh
knows 'em all by name?

777
00:56:22,350 --> 00:56:23,684
Don't be afraid, son.

778
00:56:24,252 --> 00:56:25,887
I won't let anything
happen to you.

779
00:56:26,921 --> 00:56:28,122
Load that up.

780
00:56:30,358 --> 00:56:31,458
[gun cocks]

781
00:56:46,207 --> 00:56:47,575
Something happens to me...

782
00:56:48,342 --> 00:56:50,344
it's gonna be just you
to take care of your mom.

783
00:57:04,692 --> 00:57:05,726
You see it?

784
00:57:06,560 --> 00:57:07,929
Breathe.

785
00:57:10,430 --> 00:57:11,599
Pull the trigger.

786
00:57:14,568 --> 00:57:15,603
Pull it.

787
00:57:18,839 --> 00:57:20,041
-Jake.
-[trigger clicks]

788
00:57:24,278 --> 00:57:25,346
You did it.

789
00:57:26,914 --> 00:57:28,983
Courage under stress.
Very good.

790
00:57:30,618 --> 00:57:31,752
Proud of you, son.

791
00:57:37,892 --> 00:57:39,727
[branch snaps]
[leaves rustle]

792
00:57:41,662 --> 00:57:43,564
Get behind me.
Get down, get down.

793
00:57:45,465 --> 00:57:47,001
You got three seconds
to come out!

794
00:57:48,336 --> 00:57:49,337
Three.

795
00:57:50,705 --> 00:57:51,706
Two.

796
00:57:53,174 --> 00:57:54,175
One!

797
00:57:54,942 --> 00:57:56,043
[gunshot]

798
00:58:15,963 --> 00:58:16,964
Jake!

799
00:58:24,271 --> 00:58:27,308
[wolf snarls]

800
00:58:29,343 --> 00:58:30,678
[snarls]

801
00:58:31,712 --> 00:58:33,381
[snarls and barks]

802
00:58:34,615 --> 00:58:35,683
Jake.

803
00:58:36,784 --> 00:58:37,818
Don't move.

804
00:58:47,928 --> 00:58:49,130
Stay where you are, Jake.

805
00:59:01,776 --> 00:59:02,743
[flesh squishing]

806
00:59:02,910 --> 00:59:03,744
Ahh!

807
00:59:08,015 --> 00:59:09,717
[wolf whines]

808
00:59:18,893 --> 00:59:20,728
[Chris gasps loudly]

809
00:59:27,268 --> 00:59:29,203
What happened?
What happened, Chris?

810
00:59:29,603 --> 00:59:31,038
Chris, what happened?

811
00:59:31,238 --> 00:59:32,807
Come on. Okay, sit.

812
00:59:33,007 --> 00:59:33,974
Sit, sit, sit, sit.

813
00:59:34,141 --> 00:59:36,644
Okay, okay, okay.
Okay, baby.

814
00:59:36,877 --> 00:59:37,910
Jake, go to the bathroom.

815
00:59:37,912 --> 00:59:39,747
Go get my first aid kit,
uh, the toiletry kit.

816
00:59:39,914 --> 00:59:40,981
And some towels please.

817
00:59:41,282 --> 00:59:42,450
Baby, what happened?

818
00:59:42,616 --> 00:59:44,652
What happened, baby?
Tell me what happened.

819
00:59:52,259 --> 00:59:54,395
-[Tara] Lift up.
-[Chris groans]

820
00:59:56,163 --> 00:59:57,532
Someone was out there.

821
00:59:58,533 --> 00:59:59,900
Before we got attacked.

822
01:00:01,536 --> 01:00:02,571
Watching us.

823
01:00:02,937 --> 01:00:04,405
Are you sure it wasn't...

824
01:00:05,206 --> 01:00:06,707
just someone in the woods?

825
01:00:06,974 --> 01:00:09,009
Hiking,
like you and Jake were.

826
01:00:09,176 --> 01:00:10,211
Yeah, I'm sure.

827
01:00:11,212 --> 01:00:13,247
I yelled for 'em
to come out, they hid.

828
01:00:14,415 --> 01:00:15,950
Maybe they were afraid.

829
01:00:16,117 --> 01:00:18,619
Why would they be afraid
of a guy and his kid walking?

830
01:00:18,986 --> 01:00:20,387
Well,
you said you were yelling.

831
01:00:21,055 --> 01:00:22,323
'Cause they were following us.

832
01:00:22,490 --> 01:00:23,757
Well, how do you know
they weren't just--

833
01:00:23,924 --> 01:00:26,060
Why are you so convinced
I didn't see what I saw?

834
01:00:35,302 --> 01:00:36,403
You're all done.

835
01:00:38,439 --> 01:00:39,740
I'm gonna go wash up.

836
01:01:02,496 --> 01:01:04,498
[muffled yelling]

837
01:01:17,678 --> 01:01:19,446
Help me get outta here,
please!

838
01:01:20,080 --> 01:01:22,049
Please! It's not right!

839
01:01:22,449 --> 01:01:24,251
Please help me get outta here!

840
01:01:24,885 --> 01:01:26,954
Please don't leave me.
Don't leave me!

841
01:01:30,925 --> 01:01:31,959
[Reporter] A developing system

842
01:01:32,126 --> 01:01:33,595
is moving in tonight
from the west,

843
01:01:33,761 --> 01:01:36,397
bringing increasing cloud
cover and rising pressure

844
01:01:36,565 --> 01:01:37,765
across the region.

845
01:01:37,932 --> 01:01:40,201
Skies will darken through
the early morning hours

846
01:01:40,367 --> 01:01:41,936
as that system
continues to build.

847
01:01:42,369 --> 01:01:44,606
Winds are expected
to pick up gradually.

848
01:01:44,772 --> 01:01:46,541
Steady at first,
then shifting direction

849
01:01:46,707 --> 01:01:48,175
as the front begins
to organize.

850
01:01:48,375 --> 01:01:51,078
By midday tomorrow,
scattered thunder is likely,

851
01:01:51,245 --> 01:01:54,281
with a chance
of more sustained activity
into the evening.

852
01:01:54,448 --> 01:01:56,483
-Hey.
-Hey. Morning.

853
01:01:57,051 --> 01:01:58,520
[TV shuts off]

854
01:02:00,487 --> 01:02:01,523
Can I help you?

855
01:02:02,691 --> 01:02:04,959
Oh, just doing my rounds,
checking on things.

856
01:02:06,193 --> 01:02:07,461
There's no one here but us.

857
01:02:11,732 --> 01:02:13,400
Yeah, I heard there was
some gunshots let off

858
01:02:13,568 --> 01:02:14,501
in the woods around here.

859
01:02:16,070 --> 01:02:17,304
You asking if it was me?

860
01:02:17,771 --> 01:02:19,940
No, I already know
the answer to that one.

861
01:02:22,142 --> 01:02:23,944
Wondering more what it means.

862
01:02:24,778 --> 01:02:26,847
I'm still not sure what
all of this has to do with me.

863
01:02:27,348 --> 01:02:28,782
Really?

864
01:02:31,252 --> 01:02:32,621
You're not the first
to travel this road.

865
01:02:32,786 --> 01:02:33,988
You don't have to do it alone.

866
01:02:37,224 --> 01:02:38,459
You're trying
to get in my head.

867
01:02:38,627 --> 01:02:40,528
I'm trying to offer you
some grace here, man.

868
01:02:40,695 --> 01:02:41,596
Who are you to give me grace?

869
01:02:41,762 --> 01:02:42,863
-A friend?
-A friend.

870
01:02:43,230 --> 01:02:44,231
When did that happen?

871
01:02:44,398 --> 01:02:45,667
Maybe when some weapons
went missing

872
01:02:45,833 --> 01:02:47,067
in the gun shop parking lot.

873
01:02:47,736 --> 01:02:50,271
Or the dead wolf.
Or the-the trail of blood.

874
01:02:51,238 --> 01:02:53,140
I'd appreciate it if you
didn't come by anymore.

875
01:02:55,142 --> 01:02:56,544
Not while we're still here.

876
01:03:01,115 --> 01:03:02,717
[Keith] You think he's
connected to the case?

877
01:03:03,718 --> 01:03:05,085
[Chris] I don't know.

878
01:03:06,053 --> 01:03:07,955
Trying to put it all together.

879
01:03:09,923 --> 01:03:11,025
[Keith] What about Tara?

880
01:03:12,993 --> 01:03:14,729
It was her idea
to bring you out here.

881
01:03:16,263 --> 01:03:18,032
She got the ball rolling
on the settlement.

882
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:21,335
Between her and Hersh...

883
01:03:23,203 --> 01:03:24,506
I'm just saying.

884
01:03:26,708 --> 01:03:28,309
Gotta keep our eyes open.

885
01:03:31,412 --> 01:03:32,747
Keep Jake close.

886
01:04:01,275 --> 01:04:02,777
[whispering]

887
01:05:41,008 --> 01:05:42,042
Chris?

888
01:06:53,915 --> 01:06:56,718
[door opens and closes]

889
01:07:02,356 --> 01:07:03,390
You're up.

890
01:07:04,659 --> 01:07:05,894
I'm up.

891
01:07:09,764 --> 01:07:12,800
So, when's the, um,
big reveal?

892
01:07:13,166 --> 01:07:14,669
For
that thing you're building.

893
01:07:16,905 --> 01:07:18,305
There's nothing to reveal.

894
01:07:18,940 --> 01:07:19,941
I'm just building.

895
01:07:20,675 --> 01:07:21,609
Really.

896
01:07:22,977 --> 01:07:24,044
Well, um...

897
01:07:24,646 --> 01:07:26,548
I'd-I'd still like to see

898
01:07:27,080 --> 01:07:29,918
what you've been
so secretive about.

899
01:07:30,083 --> 01:07:31,151
It's no secret.

900
01:07:32,286 --> 01:07:33,387
It's just a workspace.

901
01:07:34,421 --> 01:07:35,924
Just a place I can be alone.

902
01:07:36,423 --> 01:07:38,158
That's it. Just like a...

903
01:07:39,994 --> 01:07:41,629
like a, like a man cave.

904
01:07:43,130 --> 01:07:44,197
A cave?

905
01:07:48,770 --> 01:07:50,070
Or cell?

906
01:07:58,546 --> 01:07:59,547
Chris, tha--

907
01:07:59,981 --> 01:08:01,549
that is not normal.

908
01:08:04,018 --> 01:08:05,687
That space was all I had here.

909
01:08:08,856 --> 01:08:09,958
That's not true.

910
01:08:10,123 --> 01:08:12,259
The only safe space...

911
01:08:12,994 --> 01:08:15,362
I had here.

912
01:08:17,364 --> 01:08:18,432
And you--

913
01:08:18,633 --> 01:08:19,867
you took that away.

914
01:08:20,167 --> 01:08:22,637
You're not in prison
anymore, Chris.

915
01:08:22,804 --> 01:08:24,271
You are not there anymore.

916
01:08:24,438 --> 01:08:27,174
You are here.
You are here with me and Jake

917
01:08:27,341 --> 01:08:28,810
and your family who loves you.

918
01:08:28,977 --> 01:08:30,177
You had no right!

919
01:08:35,984 --> 01:08:37,085
[door slams]

920
01:08:40,688 --> 01:08:42,590
[keyboard tapping]

921
01:09:06,881 --> 01:09:07,949
I'm thinking of...

922
01:09:08,650 --> 01:09:09,751
heading into town.

923
01:09:11,485 --> 01:09:13,420
[cartoons play on TV]

924
01:09:15,757 --> 01:09:16,991
Jake's outta clay.

925
01:09:17,457 --> 01:09:19,694
And we can use
a few other things too.

926
01:09:23,330 --> 01:09:24,599
You mind, uh...

927
01:09:25,833 --> 01:09:27,401
you mind if
I take Jake with me?

928
01:09:28,168 --> 01:09:29,604
You don't need my permission.

929
01:09:33,141 --> 01:09:34,374
We shouldn't be too long.

930
01:09:41,448 --> 01:09:42,950
Have you seen my phone?

931
01:09:43,818 --> 01:09:46,020
It was charging this morning.

932
01:09:46,921 --> 01:09:48,122
Before our talk.

933
01:09:49,757 --> 01:09:51,191
No. I haven't.

934
01:09:53,094 --> 01:09:54,896
I respect other
people's things.

935
01:10:00,535 --> 01:10:02,036
Okay. Come on.

936
01:10:08,910 --> 01:10:10,745
Let's get you buckled. Okay?

937
01:10:11,946 --> 01:10:12,980
Okay.

938
01:10:37,672 --> 01:10:40,174
[air hissing]

939
01:10:53,621 --> 01:10:55,255
Come on, baby.
Let's go.

940
01:10:55,890 --> 01:10:56,891
All right.

941
01:10:58,192 --> 01:10:59,292
Let's go.

942
01:11:01,195 --> 01:11:02,930
Okay, you see
Daddy coming, you knock.

943
01:11:03,097 --> 01:11:04,632
Real hard, yeah?
All right.

944
01:11:05,166 --> 01:11:07,068
You good?
Okay, I love you.

945
01:12:01,022 --> 01:12:01,923
[phone chimes]

946
01:12:16,270 --> 01:12:18,573
The car has a flat.

947
01:12:19,372 --> 01:12:20,575
The spare's flat too.

948
01:12:21,374 --> 01:12:22,743
I was thinking maybe...

949
01:12:24,879 --> 01:12:28,249
maybe Instacarting something,
but the Internet is down.

950
01:12:30,284 --> 01:12:31,285
It's fine.

951
01:12:32,320 --> 01:12:33,888
Yeah, uh, we can go tomorrow.

952
01:12:35,056 --> 01:12:35,990
Yeah?

953
01:12:37,424 --> 01:12:39,627
Come here, Jake.
Come on.

954
01:12:40,460 --> 01:12:41,729
Let's get ready for bed.

955
01:12:41,896 --> 01:12:42,730
Yeah?

956
01:12:43,197 --> 01:12:44,632
Maybe get some ice cream.

957
01:12:51,105 --> 01:12:52,740
Looks like he's okay
here with me.

958
01:12:57,778 --> 01:12:59,881
Yeah. Okay.

959
01:13:15,930 --> 01:13:17,231
[Chris] It's bad, bro.

960
01:13:19,033 --> 01:13:20,201
It's all bad.

961
01:13:22,136 --> 01:13:23,403
And Tara?

962
01:13:25,172 --> 01:13:26,374
I think she's...

963
01:13:38,085 --> 01:13:39,220
We aight.

964
01:13:39,754 --> 01:13:41,188
We good, we good.

965
01:13:45,359 --> 01:13:46,661
[Keith] The settlement.

966
01:13:47,427 --> 01:13:48,495
-[Tara] Okay.
-The millions.

967
01:13:48,663 --> 01:13:49,664
-[call dialing]
-Okay.

968
01:13:49,830 --> 01:13:51,065
-[call rings]
-Come on.

969
01:13:51,464 --> 01:13:53,000
It's why they let you out.

970
01:13:54,035 --> 01:13:55,536
It's the reason
she lured you here.

971
01:13:55,703 --> 01:13:57,271
[Man] 911.
What's your emergency?

972
01:13:57,705 --> 01:13:59,439
[Keith] Reason they're
planning to take Jake.

973
01:13:59,974 --> 01:14:01,676
[Man] 911.
What's your emergency?

974
01:14:03,911 --> 01:14:05,112
[Man] Hello?
Is anybody there?

975
01:14:05,279 --> 01:14:07,348
[Keith] They had the place.
They had the plan.

976
01:14:09,283 --> 01:14:11,252
[Keith] And with Hersh, a vet,

977
01:14:12,485 --> 01:14:14,055
they had the perfect
set of eyes.

978
01:14:21,662 --> 01:14:24,464
[voicemail beeps]
You have two new messages.

979
01:14:24,999 --> 01:14:27,868
Hello, this is Dr. Salinas,
resident psychiatrist

980
01:14:28,035 --> 01:14:30,204
at Western State
Correctional Facility.

981
01:14:30,371 --> 01:14:32,974
I received your message
regarding Christopher Newborn

982
01:14:33,140 --> 01:14:34,442
and was deeply troubled.

983
01:14:34,608 --> 01:14:36,110
Tara was the last piece.

984
01:14:37,278 --> 01:14:38,446
She found a perfect place,

985
01:14:38,612 --> 01:14:40,314
and even a lawyer
to start the paperwork.

986
01:14:41,282 --> 01:14:42,817
She just had to play her part.

987
01:14:43,050 --> 01:14:44,719
The money gets split
three ways.

988
01:14:44,919 --> 01:14:46,854
[Dr. Salinas] There are
a few things you should know.

989
01:14:47,021 --> 01:14:48,155
Things you should've
been told

990
01:14:48,322 --> 01:14:50,024
before he ever
left the facility.

991
01:14:50,424 --> 01:14:52,360
Everything you thought
about it was true.

992
01:14:52,626 --> 01:14:53,928
You knew it all along.

993
01:14:55,363 --> 01:14:56,731
We knew it all along.

994
01:15:07,341 --> 01:15:08,743
[call rings]

995
01:15:08,909 --> 01:15:10,144
Hi, Dr. Salinas.

996
01:15:10,411 --> 01:15:12,013
It's Tara Bishop.
I called you earlier.

997
01:15:12,179 --> 01:15:13,214
I just got your message.

998
01:15:13,681 --> 01:15:16,550
No, no. No, I'm alone.
He's inside with my son.

999
01:15:17,284 --> 01:15:18,486
And there's something else.

1000
01:15:20,654 --> 01:15:22,023
I told you I hadn't
talked to Tara

1001
01:15:22,189 --> 01:15:23,391
since the night
you went away.

1002
01:15:25,626 --> 01:15:26,627
That's not true.

1003
01:15:28,129 --> 01:15:29,063
Yeah, but--

1004
01:15:31,165 --> 01:15:32,266
What are you saying?

1005
01:15:36,604 --> 01:15:37,705
Well...

1006
01:15:40,174 --> 01:15:41,208
Tara...

1007
01:15:42,276 --> 01:15:43,277
and...

1008
01:15:44,513 --> 01:15:45,780
and I, we...

1009
01:15:48,716 --> 01:15:49,984
Me and her...

1010
01:15:53,054 --> 01:15:54,355
I didn't plan on it.

1011
01:15:55,222 --> 01:15:56,357
Neither of us did.

1012
01:15:59,293 --> 01:16:00,529
But...

1013
01:16:02,997 --> 01:16:04,098
It happened.

1014
01:16:05,733 --> 01:16:07,001
A couple times.

1015
01:16:10,604 --> 01:16:11,672
Then a lot more.

1016
01:16:13,474 --> 01:16:14,509
Oh--

1017
01:16:15,843 --> 01:16:17,078
[Keith] It was a mistake.

1018
01:16:18,045 --> 01:16:19,447
But you don't need her, bro.

1019
01:16:22,349 --> 01:16:23,417
You got me.

1020
01:16:23,751 --> 01:16:24,819
You got Jake.

1021
01:16:29,223 --> 01:16:30,224
Tara.

1022
01:16:31,292 --> 01:16:32,561
She's just a whore.

1023
01:16:34,328 --> 01:16:35,496
A lyin',

1024
01:16:36,030 --> 01:16:37,064
plottin',

1025
01:16:37,498 --> 01:16:38,599
disloyal,

1026
01:16:39,100 --> 01:16:40,000
opportunist--

1027
01:16:40,968 --> 01:16:42,236
-[crashing sound]
-[men groan]

1028
01:16:49,910 --> 01:16:51,345
-[groaning]
-[punch lands]

1029
01:16:52,581 --> 01:16:53,647
-[bone snaps]
-[Chris screams]

1030
01:16:55,783 --> 01:16:57,251
[fighting noises]

1031
01:17:08,696 --> 01:17:10,599
[yelling]

1032
01:17:14,702 --> 01:17:16,804
I gave my life for you!

1033
01:17:18,906 --> 01:17:20,141
Nine years!

1034
01:17:20,307 --> 01:17:21,942
For what you did!

1035
01:17:24,445 --> 01:17:25,679
You come over here, Jake.

1036
01:17:26,013 --> 01:17:27,549
-Come on over here.
-Jake, don't move!

1037
01:17:27,715 --> 01:17:28,517
Hey!

1038
01:17:28,682 --> 01:17:29,551
You stay put.

1039
01:17:30,217 --> 01:17:31,450
Jake! Come here.

1040
01:17:31,452 --> 01:17:34,288
That's your plan all along?
Try to take my son from me?

1041
01:17:34,455 --> 01:17:36,257
Jake, you come over here
with me, it's okay.

1042
01:17:36,423 --> 01:17:37,592
Jake. Come here.

1043
01:17:38,527 --> 01:17:39,460
Now.

1044
01:17:40,127 --> 01:17:40,995
Come with me.

1045
01:17:45,366 --> 01:17:47,101
-[gunshot]
-[loud thud]

1046
01:17:49,571 --> 01:17:51,071
He tried to take Jake!

1047
01:17:51,705 --> 01:17:53,107
Your plan won't work.

1048
01:17:53,474 --> 01:17:55,075
-Chris...
-It's not gonna work!

1049
01:17:56,343 --> 01:17:57,344
Okay.

1050
01:18:00,447 --> 01:18:01,448
[Tara] Okay.

1051
01:18:02,950 --> 01:18:03,951
Baby.

1052
01:18:05,319 --> 01:18:06,353
Chris.

1053
01:18:07,721 --> 01:18:09,558
Put the gun down,
baby, please.

1054
01:18:10,691 --> 01:18:12,527
No one is trying to take Jake.

1055
01:18:12,693 --> 01:18:14,261
You didn't think he'd
find out what you did?

1056
01:18:14,495 --> 01:18:16,197
-Chris.
-Answer him.

1057
01:18:17,264 --> 01:18:18,799
-Please.
-She's still in it.

1058
01:18:18,966 --> 01:18:19,867
-Tara.
-Okay, Jake--

1059
01:18:20,034 --> 01:18:21,001
Don't!

1060
01:18:23,470 --> 01:18:24,738
Baby, listen to me.

1061
01:18:25,873 --> 01:18:26,941
Okay?

1062
01:18:29,143 --> 01:18:30,911
I spoke to Dr. Salinas.

1063
01:18:31,078 --> 01:18:31,979
What?

1064
01:18:32,547 --> 01:18:33,648
Shoot her.

1065
01:18:34,148 --> 01:18:35,783
She told me what you were
going through.

1066
01:18:38,653 --> 01:18:39,787
About Keith.

1067
01:18:40,321 --> 01:18:41,286
Shoot her.

1068
01:18:41,288 --> 01:18:43,157
Keith told me everything
about you and him.

1069
01:18:43,324 --> 01:18:44,593
-Chris.
-He's been here with me

1070
01:18:44,758 --> 01:18:45,759
the whole time.

1071
01:18:46,827 --> 01:18:49,363
Keith died of an overdose.

1072
01:18:49,664 --> 01:18:51,432
New Year's Eve,
seven years ago.

1073
01:18:53,500 --> 01:18:55,436
-Chris.
-I wrote you a letter.

1074
01:18:56,971 --> 01:18:58,105
